---
# Inherits the project configuration and relaxes exactly one family of checks.
#
# These are console programs whose entire job is formatted output, and
# `printf` is the clearest way to lay out a fixed-width report. The
# alternatives are iostream manipulator soup or hand-padded `std::format`
# calls, neither of which is safer here -- every format string is a literal in
# the same function as its arguments.
#
# Scoped to this directory rather than disabled project-wide: the library and
# the tests keep the check, where a vararg call really would be a smell.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays
